{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/971746-viking-age-werewolf-and-trolls","id":971746,"title":"Viking age werewolf and trolls.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T21:21:52-07:00","id":971746,"title":"Viking age werewolf and trolls.","content":"Theres something a bit depressing about pushing everything to 'the hisil did it.' What would stats for trolls look like?<br /> <br /> 10 health, 5 strength? Weakness to religious song as a ban and sunlight as a bane? <br /> <br /> I bet they have a write up in changeling, yet I was thinking of something a bit more mundane... something actually cryptid instead of spirit claimed monstrosities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:46:56-07:00","id":971757,"title":"","content":"I've always found it depressing that so many people want to reject the Hisil out of hand.<br /> <br /> Yeah Changeling probably has a few hobgoblins but I'd probably look for stats of Beast, from the sort of Beauty and the Beast expys in one of the books. But since it's just really a brute you shouldn't have a hard time writing it up yourself, or finding a variant somewhere else. Slasher has the Tin Angel who would fit. Add two Sizes, two Health, a point of Armor and take away the Thaumatechnology and you have a big brute. <br /> <br /> Add Dread Powers as you want to fit whatever fiction the troll comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-18-2016, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:05:04-07:00","id":971764,"title":"","content":"I was going for strait up scandinavian mythos.<br /> <br /> though honestly if I was going to go hisil involvement I'd do something similar to what was seen with Stand Still Stay Silent (sssscomic.com) for a claimed sort of beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:47:06-07:00","id":971777,"title":"","content":"You can also use Horror rules from <b>CoD </b>Rulebook - I use it for everything to much 'fleshier' to normal Ephemeral Beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:47:53-07:00","id":971837,"title":"","content":"Here is a fellow I wrote up some time ago - I think he might be useful for you.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The Black Forest Troll</b><br /> <br /> The creature known as \u201cThe Black Forest Troll\u201d has haunted the most remote reaches of Germany\u2019s Black Forest since medieval times and perhaps even longer. While most people who live and work in the Black forest of heard tales of the creature, most dismiss it has fairy tales told to children and gullible tourists. However, the Troll is quite real. Eyewitnesses describe a creature with the physique of a primitive man, but of gigantic proportion. His hide is leathery, warty, and covered in coarse hair. And his continence is crude and fantastical ugly, with beady eyes and a wide mouth filled with crooked, yellowed teeth. And true to the legends, he has a taste for human flesh. He has been alive for centuries, and has a surprising degree of intelligence and cunning, often capturing his prey alive and chatting with them for hours before devouring them.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Sly; <b>Vice: </b>Gluttonous<br /> <b>Aspiration: </b>Staying well Fed<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 8, Dexterity 3, Stamina 7<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 4(Climb), Brawl 5, Crafts 1, Intimidation 4, Socialize 1, Stealth 4 (Forest), Survival 4(Tracking), Weaponry 2 (Improvised)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Iron Stamina 3, Style: Relentless Assault 3, Trained Observer 3<br /> <b>Potency: </b>4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 7<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17 (Species 6)<br /> <b>Health: </b>14<br /> <b>Banes: </b>Fire<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Bite/Claw [+0L melee; 13 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Armored Hide, <b><i>Elusive*,</i> <i>Hideous Strength*,</i> </b>Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Elusive</span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: Creatures with this dread power only ever appear on camera as a blurred silhouette of their actual shape. Humanoid monsters can easily be mistaken for humans or upright bears, while unusually large creatures blend into the scenery. Humans have a hard time remembering exact detail about creatures they encounter. Rolls to accurately describe or recall such events are made at a \u20133 modifier.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hideous Strength:</i></b> The creature\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, the Horror can increase its Strength by its Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, it adds its Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:10:24-07:00","id":971930,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's exactly like what I was thinking of. I may do a whole slew of creatures as trolls are fairly variable in the Scandinavian variety. Including giants and the such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:53:17-07:00","id":972140,"title":"","content":"Beasts (from <i>Beast: The Primordial</i>) could function as trolls.<br /> <br /> Ogres (from <i>Changeling: The Lost</i>) could function as trolls.<br /> <br /> Certain types of spirits and/or Claimed could easily be the basis of several troll myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:16:44-07:00","id":980809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/971746-viking-age-werewolf-and-trolls?p=971764#post971764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> though honestly if I was going to go hisil involvement I'd do something similar to what was seen with Stand Still Stay Silent (sssscomic.com) for a claimed sort of beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bStand Still Stay Silent is what a lot of my Hisil and Claimed look like anyway, no need for Scandinavia as a setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bBeyond that... sometimes there's just weird shit in an area that doesn't easily match up to existing Forsaken classifications, like the <i>leshy </i>in Poland. I think, for fun, I'd make trolls as <i>like </i>Claimed but with a major difference - they have become subjugated by their own emotions given spiritual power and sentience. A troll is what you get when someone's Gluttony or Pride or Hatred literally takes them over, physically and spiritually via processes that the Forsaken are not entirely clear on - no spirits involved, not even conceptuals. They look like Claimed but most definitely aren't - and act as wellsprings of their emotional resonance, drawing spirits into their orbit through whom the trolls can perform simple 'magic' via commanding them. The longer you leave a troll, the bigger and uglier it gets - I'd run with an age-based Size and stats modifier - unlike Claimed where it's the spirit's power that dictates how potent the Claimed amalgam is, with a troll it just gets nastier and larger the longer you leave it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:54:06-07:00","id":980957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/971746-viking-age-werewolf-and-trolls?p=980809#post980809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bStand Still Stay Silent is what a lot of my Hisil and Claimed look like anyway, no need for Scandinavia as a setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bBeyond that... sometimes there's just weird shit in an area that doesn't easily match up to existing Forsaken classifications, like the <i>leshy </i>in Poland. I think, for fun, I'd make trolls as <i>like </i>Claimed but with a major difference - they have become subjugated by their own emotions given spiritual power and sentience. A troll is what you get when someone's Gluttony or Pride or Hatred literally takes them over, physically and spiritually via processes that the Forsaken are not entirely clear on - no spirits involved, not even conceptuals. They look like Claimed but most definitely aren't - and act as wellsprings of their emotional resonance, drawing spirits into their orbit through whom the trolls can perform simple 'magic' via commanding them. The longer you leave a troll, the bigger and uglier it gets - I'd run with an age-based Size and stats modifier - unlike Claimed where it's the spirit's power that dictates how potent the Claimed amalgam is, with a troll it just gets nastier and larger the longer you leave it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like varg vikernes interpretation of ettins. This is good stuff, but I would expect nothing less from a seasoned writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}